{
  "id": "world-championships",
  "name": "World Championships",
  "category": "event",
  "description": {
    "text": "The Pokémon World Championships is the game's invitational tournament, held each August. Since 2004, the first run by Pokémon Organized Play, every year has handed out two kinds of card. Each competitor gets the year's participation card: Tropical Wind (2004 and 2007 to 2009), Tropical Tidal Wave (2005, 2006 and 2010), Tropical Beach (2011 and 2012), Champions Festival (2013 to 2022) and Paradise Resort (from 2023), for many years in seven languages. The 2004 card began the habit of putting Psyduck in the picture. Staff get a Staff copy, and the best finishers copies stamped with their placing: Top Sixteen up to Finalist in 2004, from Top Thirty-Two in 2005, and up to Champion from 2012.\n\nThe top three of each age division get trophy cards, No. 1, No. 2 and No. 3 Trainer, and the top four from 2013. Their Pikachu with a cup on a podium, first drawn for 2004, was used until 2013; 5ban Graphics' full-art Pikachu cheering beside a cup in confetti followed from 2014 to 2022, and a new picture from 2023. There were no World Championships in 2020 and 2021, which were canceled during the COVID-19 pandemic.",
